From 76377538a1a2923f20dba20fc453d84ae52f4561 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:19:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gemini): the session total adds the turns' breakdowns
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

provider::sum_usage added the counters of every turn (sub-agent turns
included) and dropped their breakdowns, so total_usage had no
output.reasoning while every turn's token_usage carried one and
extract_conversation (since c65a6b6) rebuilt a total that did. The
accounting contract (Σ steps == to_view total == extracted total) did not
hold for the gemini set. sum_usage now adds breakdowns class by class,
the one loop over main and sub-agent turns sharing add_usage.

The gemini known-defect gemini-total-usage-drops-breakdowns is retired:
known_defects@gemini.snap is [], ir@gemini.snap gains output.reasoning 489
on total_usage, nothing else moves. Unit test
test_total_usage_sums_breakdowns.
---
 crates/toolpath-gemini/src/provider.rs        | 85 ++++++++++++-------
 .../toolpath-goldens/snapshots/ir@gemini.snap |  7 +-
 .../snapshots/known_defects@gemini.snap       | 18 +---
 crates/toolpath-goldens/src/defects.rs        | 10 ---
 4 files changed, 60 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/toolpath-gemini/src/provider.rs b/crates/toolpath-gemini/src/provider.rs
index ead4700a..4ce7b407 100644
--- a/crates/toolpath-gemini/src/provider.rs
